{
 "id": "mortgage_offer",
 "request": "Mortgage applications arrive by webhook with application_id, applicant_email, amount and property_value. Get the applicant's credit score from the bureau (the applicant id is the application id). Below 580: email the applicant that we can't offer a mortgage, set the application's status to 'declined' in ops_db mortgage_applications, and stop. Otherwise an underwriter decides: a task for UNDERWRITER_EMAIL, due in 2 days, showing the amount, property value, loan-to-value and score, where they enter approved_amount and conditions. If the underwriter hasn't decided in 2 days, email them a reminder and give them one more day (a second task, same form). If that runs out too, the head of lending (HEAD_OF_LENDING_EMAIL) decides with the same form, due in 1 day, and if nobody decides it is declined. If the approved amount is over 500,000, two credit committee members (CREDIT_COMMITTEE_EMAIL) must also approve, one after the other (four eyes), seeing the approved amount and conditions. Any rejection: email the applicant that we can't offer a mortgage and set status 'declined'. Once approved: email the applicant the offer with the approved amount and the conditions, and send the offer for e-signature. Then check the signature once a day, up to 5 times. When it's signed: book the mortgage for the approved amount, and in one transaction set the application's status to 'booked' and add an audit_log row (entity 'mortgage', the application id, action 'booked'); then email the applicant a welcome. After each of the first four checks that finds it unsigned, email the applicant a reminder to sign. If the fifth check still finds it unsigned, cancel the envelope, email the applicant that the offer has expired, and set status 'expired'.",
 "apis": [
  "bureau.yaml",
  "esign.yaml",
  "mortgages.yaml"
 ],
 "tables": {},
 "expect": {
  "trigger": "Webhook",
  "must_have_types": [
   "Approval",
   "Wait",
   "Postgres",
   "SendEmail"
  ],
  "must_call": [
   "bureau.creditScore",
   "esign.createEnvelope",
   "esign.getEnvelope",
   "esign.cancelEnvelope",
   "mortgages.book"
  ],
  "max_nodes": 45,
  "min_types": {
   "Approval": 5
  }
 },
 "hidden_tests": [
